    "summary": "Model generated successfully and passed L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\n**Root cause of the failure:** The stored `lane.qk` decision was 10.5 kN/m, the Class I base value, but the bridge is Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015). Clause JTGD60-4.3.1-qk requires qk = 10.5 x 0.75 = 7.875 kN/m for Class II. Check L2-1 re-executes each governing formula against the model parameters and found the lane uniform load inconsistent with its provenance decision, so it flagged the model. The instance already correctly recorded load_class=II; the error was purely in the accepted decision value.\n\n**Repair:** Re-proposed `lane.qk = 7.875 kN/m` (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-qk, INPUT:deck.load_class), which was accepted; regenerated the model.\n\n**Final model:** Single simply supported span, spine-beam 2D idealization. Precast prestressed small-box girders, 5 per span, combined section A = 5.303 m^2, I = 1.258 m^4, Ec = 32500 MPa, gamma = 26 kN/m^3, w = 137.87 kN/m, m = 14.05 t/m. Plain laminated elastomeric bearings at both abutments (10 per line, 300x350 mm, 4x8 mm layers): S = 10.096, Kv = 1.416e7 kN/m, Kh = 3.28e4 kN/m per line, vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free. Live load: 4 lanes, xi = 0.67, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 232.5 kN, mu = 0.241 (from f1).\n\n**Key results:** f1 = 4.272 Hz (next modes 16.90, 37.30 Hz); self-weight reactions 1723.3 kN per support; self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kNm; live-load max positive moment 6878.4 kNm."
